Sentinel for Debian/Ubuntu
==========================

What this package is
--------------------

The Go CONTROL PLANE, statically linked, in /usr/bin:

    agentctl         the CLI — everything the product does, from the terminal
    control-api      HTTP control plane + the browser UI (ADR-064)
    store-gateway    persistence for runs/scenarios/tests/chats/results/config
    orchestrator     run-control gRPC (pause/resume/takeover)
    report-service   report generation

What this package is NOT
------------------------

It is not a runnable test stack. A real browser run needs three more things on
this host, none of which a .deb should be silently dragging in:

    Python 3.11+ and uv     the planning / healing brain
    Node 24+                the Playwright executor
    Playwright browsers     `npx playwright install chromium`

Two honest ways to get a working run:

  1. Container — the whole stack in one image, nothing else to install:

         docker run --rm ghcr.io/alexgromer/sentinel:latest --help

  2. This package as a CLIENT — agentctl drives a control-api that has the
     stack, on another host or in a container:

         agentctl --help

Starting control-api as a service
---------------------------------

Nothing starts on install. control-api mints a bearer token on first start and
can serve a UI that starts runs; that is the operator's call, not the packager's.

    sudoedit /etc/sentinel/control-api.env      # at minimum, review the bind address
    sudo systemctl enable --now sentinel-control-api
    journalctl -u sentinel-control-api -f       # the startup line carries the UI link

The unit runs under a systemd DynamicUser with /var/lib/sentinel as its state
directory, so no system account is created and nothing is left behind on purge.

Configuration
-------------

/etc/sentinel/control-api.env is a conffile — dpkg preserves your edits across
upgrades. Its variables are the same CONTROL_API_* / LLM_* names used by the
container and by `agentctl` (ADR-107: one configuration model, three complete
projections — CLI, HTTP, UI/files). There is deliberately no packaging-only
configuration surface.

Verifying what you installed
----------------------------

Every release asset is checksummed and signed keyless with cosign:

    cosign verify-blob sentinel_<version>_<arch>.deb \
      --bundle sentinel_<version>_<arch>.deb.cosign.bundle \
      --certificate-identity-regexp 'https://github.com/AlexGromer/sentinel/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/tags/v.*' \
      --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com

 -- AlexGromer
